redumper-mpf (732-2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Add aarch64 (arm64) support: the linux-arm64 upstream binary travels as a
    Debtransform-Files extra and debian/rules swaps it in on arm64 builds
    (Architecture is now amd64 arm64). Ships UNTESTED on arm64 -- no hardware
    drive-access proof; the repackage path is architecture-neutral.

 -- gmipf <gmipf64@gmail.com>  Sat, 18 Jul 2026 01:20:00 +0000

redumper-mpf (732-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Initial package. Pinned-build compatibility package carrying upstream
    redumper b732 as /usr/bin/redumper-mpf -- the build MPF's publish-nix.sh
    bundles. The mpf packages point their configuration at it, so an MPF dump
    runs the dumper build its upstream actually tested with.
  * The pin exists even though the rolling redumper package carries the very same
    build today. That equality is an accident of timing, not something to lean on:
    the rolling package moves. The day b733 is released, an MPF pointed at the
    rolling package would silently dump with a build it was never tested against,
    and MPF has no version check of any kind -- it reads whatever version it finds
    out of the log and writes it into the submission. When MPF bundles a new
    build, a new redumper<N> is generated and MPF is repointed at it.
  * Co-installable with the rolling redumper package and with redumper-rgui
    (redumper-gui's pin): the build number is in the binary name, so no files
    overlap. No manpage on purpose -- the rolling package carries redumper(1);
    this is a compatibility build, not a replacement.

 -- gmipf <gmipf64@gmail.com>  Tue, 14 Jul 2026 03:30:00 +0200
